{"step_index":1363,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T17:25:43Z","thinking":"**Analyzing PanResponder Issues**\n\nI've been looking into `DialerHudScreen.tsx`, specifically the `onStartShouldSetPanResponder` function. It seems this is intercepting user taps, preventing interactions with certain buttons. I've confirmed this with the \"View Original Report Card,\" \"Dial,\" and detail expansion buttons, as well as during scrolling, which is not ideal.\n\n\n**Refining PanResponder Logic**\n\nI've determined `onStartShouldSetPanResponder: () => true` blocks vertical scrolling.  To fix, I'm refactoring the `PanResponder` to adhere to gesture best practices. Specifically, I'm implementing `onMoveShouldSetPanResponder` to only capture horizontal gestures exceeding 10px and exceeding vertical movement. The provided code implements handling the \"dial\" and \"skip\" actions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\brorm\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\snap-dialer\\\\src\\\\screens\\\\DialerHudScreen.tsx\"","EndLine":"510","StartLine":"475","toolAction":"\"Viewing Animated.View in DialerHudScreen.tsx\"","toolSummary":"\"View Animated.View in DialerHudScreen\""}}]}
